~ start
do start_talking()
do disable_movement()
Forester: So. You found the key.
- Why did you bury it? Why block the way at all?
	Forester: Because I hoped nobody would ever need to find it. That barricade wasn't spite. It was to keep something else in.
	Forester: [wait=1] Past a certain point, the forest has been wrong for a long time now. Wrong in a way that spreads, if you let it get behind you.
	Forester: Sealing the path was the only thing I knew how to do about it. Didn't hold forever, I suppose.
- The blacksmith made you sound like a menace.
	Forester: [[Good.|That was rather the idea.|Let them talk.]] Better they're afraid of an old man in the woods than go looking for what I was actually guarding against.
	Forester: [wait=1] You're not the first to get past me, either. A stranger came through months back, asking odd questions about the trees. He never came back down.
	Forester: I should have buried that key deeper.
Forester: The way on is past the rubble, if you're set on it. Mind yourself down there.
do stop_talking()
do enable_movement()
=> END
